The Credit Card Customer Segmentation dataset contains information about customers’ credit card usage and financial behavior. 
It includes features such as account balance, purchases, cash advances, credit limits, payment amounts, and transaction frequency. 
The dataset is commonly used for clustering and customer segmentation tasks in machine learning. By analyzing these features, businesses can 
group customers based on spending habits and financial activity. The dataset helps companies understand customer behavior, identify high-value customers, 
and improve marketing strategies. Since there is no target variable, it is mainly used for unsupervised learning techniques 
  such as K-Means clustering and exploratory data analysis.
